== Notes ==
''More details on these pickups and how they work can be found [[Health|here]].''
* Unless an item effect specifically states it, a Red Heart always has the chance to be replaced by a Soul, Black, or Eternal Heart.
* If Heart pickups are created by item, card, or pill effects in certain {{r|Super Secret Room}} layouts, they will be forced to spawn as a specific heart type (e. g. all hearts will be Black Hearts). There are layouts corresponding to Red, Soul, Black, Eternal and Rotten Hearts.
* If Isaac's health bar is filled with Soul Hearts, picking up a Black Heart will replace the topmost Soul Heart.
** If Isaac's health bar is filled up to 11 1/2 (Soul/Black) Hearts with the last one being half a Black Heart, picking up a Black Heart will fill that one and convert a full Soul Heart to a Black Heart (therefore adding half a Black Heart and converting a Soul Heart).
** Collecting a Soul Heart with half a Black Heart left will complete the Black Heart, and add half a Soul Heart. The reverse is also true.
* {{dlc|a}} If Gold Hearts have not been unlocked yet, they be replaced by random Heart pickups in any room layouts containing them.
** {{dlc+|r}} If Rotten Hearts have not been unlocked yet, they will always be replaced by Half Red Hearts ({{s|Corpse}} themed {{r|Super Secret Room}}, etc.).{{dlc-}}
* {{dlc|a+}} Eternal Hearts take half a heart of damage without counting as a hit for {{r|Devil Room}} / {{r|Angel Room}} purposes.
* {{dlc|a+}} Taking Red Heart damage in a Bone Heart Container does not lower the chance of the Angel Room or Devil Room appearing. Breaking an empty Bone Heart will not either.
** {{c|The Forgotten}} is the only exception, as breaking a Bone Heart while playing as him will affect the chance.
* {{dlc|a+}} Bone Hearts cannot be broken if filled with at least a Half Red Heart, even if a full heart of damage is taken. This can be abused to repeatedly pay a half-red heart to step on a spike in a {{r|Sacrifice Room}}, for example.
* {{dlc|r}} Rotten Hearts are only donated to the {{Machine|Blood Donation Machine}} after all Red Hearts are depleted.
* {{dlc|r}} Losing Rotten Hearts does not lower the chance of the Angel Room or Devil Room appearing.
* {{dlc|r}} If after clearing a room the number of Blue Flies Isaac has is less than 2× the number of Rotten Hearts in Isaac's health, additional Blue Flies are spawned so that these numbers are equal (e. g. if Isaac has 3 Rotten Hearts and 4 Blue Flies upon clearing a room, 2 Blue Flies will spawn). Otherwise, no Blue Flies will spawn.
* {{i|Bag of Crafting}} will treat double hearts as two heart pickups. Blended Hearts will be treated as a Soul Heart and a Red Heart.
* The probabilities in the table refer to the kind of heart that is generated by the game when a heart is spawned with a subtype of 0 (i.e. a random heart).
* {{dlc|r+}} In [[Online (open beta)|Online Co-op]], dead ghost characters can pick up an Eternal Heart to instantly revive themselves.

